{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7cePz84EwNEkSUbwjJxa5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"f91a68e8c8dcdef4969050d70ac6d9c7e1bb5792\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T11:32:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Properly handle the manifest returned via pacote\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3b9970b4c3f70749ecb5421e4d14de412c35ee70\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T14:37:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Mitigate malicious tarballs in assemble command\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2edf609e742b5517239da376db482747d5da5eb9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T16:21:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Fail assemble by default if things are obviously broken (#1795)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:13:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a distribution-controlled version property (#1815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6edb9b41a9fadce4f3b5cf4818382c671be1897a\",\"date\":\"2026-04-08T17:20:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Upgrade the CLI and add comprehensive tests (#1735)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"929cd794322f4f55f340fb09850acc63e68700ed\",\"date\":\"2026-04-02T15:03:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Updates to openmrs CLI (#1729)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a7f3e474745165248e395f9081641ce4a1e20154\",\"date\":\"2025-07-11T11:01:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Restore the ability to merge multiple configuration files\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"75293696602b6aa61341bd50357b8cda9f33086f\",\"date\":\"2025-06-25T10:56:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Update TypeDoc and TypeScript (#1406)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5e321cf8164f7b4df88ae857751822d368b23af7\",\"date\":\"2025-06-11T22:26:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix assemble prompt logic by using unique keys (#1394)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Samuel Male\",\"authorEmail\":\"samuelsmalek@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"777c551525d768c750504fbaf905a53d6af2ae3d\",\"date\":\"2025-06-03T13:50:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Assemble shouldn't break if very numbers aren't specified (#1382)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3a27e7c23c9e77c4ee85a5b96f5260160e6e9cb8\",\"date\":\"2025-05-23T13:19:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Re-work Framework packages for lighter-weight builds (#1346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fba6e8f0c2837fe484236ada0cf528141e9520d4\",\"date\":\"2025-03-21T01:49:28+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Use node protocol for builtin node modules (#1319)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Shivam Sharma\",\"authorEmail\":\"meshivam81@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"ce1346deab8beb20032aec6dff88823ae00c8332\",\"date\":\"2024-09-26T16:24:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix merging configuration files to properly call readFile\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"283e859172aedd89a9a0e6675d389d91dbe3ea3e\",\"date\":\"2024-07-31T14:33:48-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix various tooling issues in core\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":37}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06dc87a3-eea2-4a8b-8687-e605f24b3454","uuid":"71d5265b-88bc-4f6b-ba9e-f2a15dc21711","timestamp":"2026-10-23T14:53:22.713Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"f91a68e8c8dcdef4969050d70ac6d9c7e1bb5792\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T11:32:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Properly handle the manifest returned via pacote\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3b9970b4c3f70749ecb5421e4d14de412c35ee70\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T14:37:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Mitigate malicious tarballs in assemble command\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2edf609e742b5517239da376db482747d5da5eb9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T16:21:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Fail assemble by default if things are obviously broken (#1795)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:13:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a distribution-controlled version property (#1815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6edb9b41a9fadce4f3b5cf4818382c671be1897a\",\"date\":\"2026-04-08T17:20:24-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Upgrade the CLI and add comprehensive tests (#1735)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"929cd794322f4f55f340fb09850acc63e68700ed\",\"date\":\"2026-04-02T15:03:40-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Updates to openmrs CLI (#1729)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a7f3e474745165248e395f9081641ce4a1e20154\",\"date\":\"2025-07-11T11:01:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Restore the ability to merge multiple configuration files\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"75293696602b6aa61341bd50357b8cda9f33086f\",\"date\":\"2025-06-25T10:56:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Update TypeDoc and TypeScript (#1406)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5e321cf8164f7b4df88ae857751822d368b23af7\",\"date\":\"2025-06-11T22:26:27+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix assemble prompt logic by using unique keys (#1394)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Samuel Male\",\"authorEmail\":\"samuelsmalek@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"777c551525d768c750504fbaf905a53d6af2ae3d\",\"date\":\"2025-06-03T13:50:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Assemble shouldn't break if very numbers aren't specified (#1382)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3a27e7c23c9e77c4ee85a5b96f5260160e6e9cb8\",\"date\":\"2025-05-23T13:19:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Re-work Framework packages for lighter-weight builds (#1346)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail