{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YCY1fWJDGKTReuJwptujzp","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\\n\\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\\nfuture version.\\n\\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\\n\\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\\n\\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\\n\\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\\n\\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\\n\\n* More clean-up\\n\\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\\n\\n* Fixup changesets\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"43e9a2e0f2e61c51c7cd40ee254da1e1c4396cc6\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T16:37:45+05:30\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5838: Implement TOTP verification page (#1844)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dilan Kavishka\",\"authorEmail\":\"109354298+dilankavishka@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:13:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a distribution-controlled version property (#1815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"671bf567c266d51e197359000b73e81d25e080a9\",\"date\":\"2026-06-08T16:58:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) O3-5645: Prevent open redirect via unvalidated returnToUrl (#1763)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* fix(esm-login-app): prevent open redirect via unvalidated returnToUrl\\n\\nValidate the \\\\\\returnToUrl\\\\ query parameter before navigating post-login.\\nAccept only same-origin URLs whose pathname falls under the configured SPA\\nbase path, rejecting external hosts, protocol-relative URLs, and paths\\noutside the SPA root.\\n\\n- Export \\\\isSafeReturnUrl\\\\ helper that parses and validates redirect targets\\n- Replace unguarded \\\\\\returnToUrl !== '/'\\\\ check with \\\\isSafeReturnUrl\\\\ guard\\n- Fall back to \\\\config.links.loginSuccess\\\\ when the URL is rejected\\n- Add 8 unit tests for \\\\isSafeReturnUrl\\\\ covering known attack vectors\\n- Add 3 integration tests for open-redirect protection in the component\\n\\n* fix(esm-login-app): simplify spa base trim in return URL check\\n\\n* fix(esm-login-app): block open-redirect via unvalidated referrer state in login\\n\\n* fix(esm-login-app): block open-redirect via unvalidated referrer in location picker\\n\\n* fix(esm-login-app): encode returnToUrl pathname to prevent query string truncation\\n\\n* test(esm-login-app): use static encoded string in change-location-link test\\n\\nUse a hardcoded pre-computed encoded URL string instead of calling\\nencodeURIComponent() inside the test assertion. This ensures the test\\nactually verifies the production output rather than tautologically\\ncomparing the same function call on both sides.\\n\\n* fix(esm-login-app): prefer node:path over path in vitest.config.ts\\n\\n* (fix) Allow any same-origin returnToUrl, not just SPA base paths\\n\\nRemoves the overly restrictive spaBase path check from isSafeReturnUrl.\\nSame-origin matching is sufficient to prevent open-redirect attacks.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <nore